Subject: [PATCH] ld/aix: keep .tbss at the TLS-relative offset

The AIX linker script intends .tdata and .tbss VMAs to represent offsets
from the TLS pointer, starting at -0x7800 for XCOFF64.  .tbss currently
inherits the location counter from .tdata, which works when .tdata is
present, but if an object only contributes .tbss then .tdata can be empty
and .tbss may instead be placed at the normal data address.  Static
R_TLS_LE relocations against .tbss then overflow their 16-bit local-exec
instruction fields.

Make .tbss start explicitly at the TLS base plus SIZEOF(.tdata), preserving
the existing .tdata/.tbss contiguity while also handling objects with only
uninitialized TLS data.

--- a/ld/scripttempl/aix.sc	2026-06-30 16:31:10.471076546 +0000
+++ b/ld/scripttempl/aix.sc	2026-07-14 18:07:55.678836833 +0000
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@
     *(.tl)
   }
 
-  .tbss : {
+  .tbss -0x7800 + SIZEOF(.tdata) : {
     *(.tbss)
     *(.ul)
   }
